>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>About World Battery Hub</h1>
      <p class="lead">World Battery Hub is a battery knowledge and data platform. It is informational, not a store.</p>

      <div class="takeaways">
        <strong>At a glance:</strong> World Battery Hub is a battery knowledge and data platform — six sites
        covering <strong>knowledge</strong> (lead-acid, lithium, basics, tools),
        <strong>data</strong> (battery groups, references), <strong>technology</strong> (engineering),
        <strong>testing</strong> (methods and standards), <strong>manufacturers</strong> and
        <strong>market intelligence</strong>. Content is researched from public sources, cross-verified, and
        labelled with its sources, standards and limitations.
      </div>

      <h2>Editorial method</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Cross-verified, not translated</strong> — content is synthesized from multiple independent sources, including Chinese and English, not translated from a single source.</li>
        <li><strong>Every number carries its standard</strong> — a <a href="/lead-acid/cca/what-is-cca/">CCA</a> value states whether it is JIS, EN, SAE or DIN; a capacity states its rate (C20, etc.).</li>
        <li><strong>Conflicts are explained</strong> — where sources disagree, the disagreement and its likely cause are stated rather than a single number being silently chosen.</li>
        <li><strong>No fabrication</strong> — if a figure cannot be traced to a source, it is stated qualitatively or marked as unknown.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What the platform covers</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/lead-acid/">Lead-acid knowledge</a> — groups, CCA, <a href="/lead-acid/agm-battery/">AGM</a>/<a href="/lead-acid/efb-battery/">EFB</a>, applications and maintenance</li>
        <li><a href="/lithium/">Lithium knowledge</a> — chemistries, cells, <a href="/lithium/what-is-bms/">BMS</a>, safety and emerging technology</li>
        <li><a href="/basics/">Battery Basics 101</a> — the six-lesson beginner path</li>
        <li><a href="/tools/">Calculators</a> — runtime, sizing and charging-time tools</li>
        <li><a href="/standards/">Standards</a> — the 15-standard directory</li>
        <li><a href="/lead-acid/products/">Product catalogue</a> — the commercial section, clearly separated</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Source hierarchy</h2>
      <p>Primary sources (manufacturer documentation, standards organizations, government data) are preferred over industry publications, which are preferred over community sources. Community sources are used to discover real-world questions, not as evidence.</p>

      <h2 id="research-desk">The World Battery Hub Research Desk</h2>
      <p>
        Content on this platform is produced by the <strong>World Battery Hub Research Desk</strong> — a
        collective editorial entity, not a named individual. We deliberately do not present a single-author
        "expert" persona, because a fabricated expert would be worse than an honest collective: the desk's
        authority rests on its <em>process</em>, which is stated and checkable, not on a name.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Research methodology</strong> — content is synthesized from multiple independent sources (including Chinese and English) and cross-verified, not translated from one source. See the full <a href="/methodology/">methodology</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Source verification</strong> — every figure carries its source and its test standard; a number without a traceable source is stated qualitatively or marked unknown.</li>
        <li><strong>Technical review process</strong> — claims are reconciled against standards documents and manufacturer datasheets before publication; conflicts are explained, not silently resolved.</li>
        <li><strong>Correction policy</strong> — errors are corrected in place and logged; the correction records the date, the old value and the new value.</li>
        <li><strong>Editorial independence</strong> — the commercial <a href="/lead-acid/products/">product catalogue</a> is separated from editorial and data content, and a commercial relationship does not change a rating, a standard or a confidence level.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        If a real engineer or researcher reviews this material in the future, that person will be credited as a
        named reviewer — a real <a href="/methodology/">Person entity</a> with their own record — never as a
        fictional byline.
      </p>

      <p class="muted">Last reviewed: 2026-09-18</p>
    </div>
  </section>
